.SH NAME
Clownfish::Integer \- Immutable 64\-bit signed integer.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    my $integer = Clownfish::Integer\->new(7);
\&    my $value = $integer\->get_value;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 1
\&    my $integer = Clownfish::Integer\->new($value);
.Ve
.PP
Return a new Integer.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBvalue\fR \- Initial value.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS get_value
.IX Subsection "get_value"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $integer\->get_value();
.Ve
.PP
Return the value of the Integer.
.SS to_f64
.IX Subsection "to_f64"
.Vb 1
\&    my $float = $integer\->to_f64();
.Ve
.PP
Convert the Integer to floating point.
.SS compare_to
.IX Subsection "compare_to"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $integer\->compare_to($other);
.Ve
.PP
Indicate whether one number is less than, equal to, or greater than
another.  Throws an exception if \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR is neither an Integer nor a
Float.
.PP
Returns: 0 if the numbers are equal, a negative number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is
less than \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR, and a positive number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is greater than
\&\f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR.
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $integer\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Return a clone of the object.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::Integer isa Clownfish::Obj.
